{number: 92}
{title: Saviour, Like a Shepherd Lead Us}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Savior, like a shepherd lead us,
Much we need Thy [Bb7] tender care;
In Thy [Eb] pleasant pastures feed us,
For our use Thy [Bb7] folds pre-[Eb] pare:
Blessed [Ab] Jesus, blessed [Eb] Jesus,
Thou hast [Bb7] bought us, Thine we [Eb] are;
Blessed [Ab] Jesus, blessed [Eb] Jesus,
Thou hast [Bb7] bought us, Thine we [Eb] are.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] We are Thine, do Thou befriend us,
Be the Guardian [Bb7] of our way;
Keep Thy [Eb] flock, from sin defend us,
Seek us when we [Bb7] go a-[Eb] stray:
Blessed [Ab] Jesus, blessed [Eb] Jesus,
Hear, O [Bb7] hear us when we [Eb] pray;
Blessed [Ab] Jesus, blessed [Eb] Jesus,
Hear, O [Bb7] hear us when we [Eb] pray.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Thou hast promised to receive us,
Poor and sinful [Bb7] though we be;
Thou hast [Eb] mercy to relieve us,
Grace to cleanse, and [Bb7] pow'r to [Eb] free:
Blessed [Ab] Jesus, blessed [Eb] Jesus,
Early [Bb7] let us turn to [Eb] Thee;
Blessed [Ab] Jesus, blessed [Eb] Jesus,
Early [Bb7] let us turn to [Eb] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
